Partition approved items into groups with **disjoint file ownership** (`references/orchestration_spec.md`); order dependent groups upstream-first. Execute group by group — delegating each bounded group that meets the delegation rule by dispatching a writing sub-agent on the EXEC tier's model, locally otherwise — under the brief: scope verbatim ("ONLY these items"), explicit file list, mechanical moves + import fixes only, no opportunistic edits, runtime via the `.env` conda env, structured result (`changed` / `ran` / `check` / `blockers`). After each group, **re-verify yourself** (compileall, import sweep, quick tests where runnable), then commit: `star-code-architect: migrate <ids> — <summary>`, staging only this skill's paths. Fail → feed the failure back, retry ≤2 → still failing: restore the group's paths via git, mark the items `blocked` in the migration record, continue with other groups.
+++ 1
Partition approved items into groups with **disjoint file ownership** (`references/orchestration_spec.md`); independent groups may run in parallel, dependent groups serially. Dispatch one `Agent` subagent (`subagent_type: general-purpose`, `model:` the EXEC tier value the opening load returned, omitted when that key is empty) per group with the brief: scope verbatim ("ONLY these items"), explicit file list, mechanical moves + import fixes only — no opportunistic edits — runtime via the `.env` conda env, structured return (`changed` / `ran` / `check` / `blockers`). After each group the **main agent re-verifies** (compileall, import sweep, quick tests where runnable), then commits: `star-code-architect: migrate <ids> — <summary>`, staging only this skill's paths. Fail → feed the failure back, retry ≤2 → still failing: restore the group's paths via git, mark the items `blocked` in the migration record, continue with other groups.
